// Title: Audio Capture via SoundRecorder
// Sigma ID: 83865853-59aa-449e-9600-74b9d89a6d6e
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: E.M. Anhaus (originally from Atomic Blue Detections, Endgame), oscd.community
// Date: 2019-10-24 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: collection, T1123
// Description: Detect attacker collecting audio via SoundRecorder application.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate audio capture by legitimate user.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1123/T1123.md
//   - https://eqllib.readthedocs.io/en/latest/analytics/f72a98cb-7b3d-4100-99c3-a138b6e9ff6e.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_soundrecorder_audio_capture.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\SoundRecorder.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/FILE"
